.IX Title "Lucy::Docs::Cookbook 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Docs::Cookbook 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Docs::Cookbook \- Lucy recipes
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The Cookbook provides thematic documentation covering some of Lucy’s
more sophisticated features.  For a step-by-step introduction to Lucy,
see Tutorial.
.SS Chapters
.IX Subsection "Chapters"
.IP \(bu 4
FastUpdates \- While index updates are fast on
average, worst-case update performance may be significantly slower. To make
index updates consistently quick, we must manually intervene to control the
process of index segment consolidation.
.IP \(bu 4
CustomQuery \- Explore Lucy’s support for
custom query types by creating a “PrefixQuery” class to handle trailing
wildcards.
.IP \(bu 4
CustomQueryParser \- Define your own custom
search query syntax using QueryParser and
Parse::RecDescent.
.SS Materials
.IX Subsection "Materials"
Some of the recipes in the Cookbook reference the completed
Tutorial application.  These materials can be
found in the \f(CW\*(C`sample\*(C'\fR directory at the root of the Lucy distribution:
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    sample/indexer.pl        # indexing app
\&    sample/search.cgi        # search app
\&    sample/us_constitution   # corpus
.Ve
